  "tagline": "In-memory columnar analytics store for unordered event data with JIT-compiled queries; dormant since 2019.",
  "description": "ViyaDB is an open-source in-memory columnar data store in C++ aimed at customer-facing ad-hoc aggregations over event data that arrives in no particular order, such as mobile attribution events. It supports random-access updates, compiles queries to machine code at runtime, rolls up older data by configurable time periods and protects itself against high-cardinality dimensions. Queries go through a REST API with a JSON query language plus basic SQL, and a documented cluster mode coordinates workers and controllers through Consul. Created by Michael Spector in 2017, it never left 1.0.0-beta (2018) and commits stopped in October 2019.",
